- D2 non-stream chat, r18 timeout shape (POST /v1/chat/completions,
  body {"model":"swe-2","max_tokens":8,"temperature":0,
  "messages":[{"role":"user","content":"ping"}]}, timeout 200 s):
  Claim: HTTP 200 with a chat.completion body (the r18 D7 cold-start
    timeout does NOT reproduce on a warm shim).
  Falsifier: timeout at 200 s (D7 reproduces even warm), or a 4xx/5xx.
  P(200) = 0.80 (warm-shim evidence is journal-level, not a completed
    non-stream draw on this shim; the r18 lane never landed one).
  Note: temperature:0 is sent deliberately — it is the r18 census shape
    (chat-devin.json request_body) and the seat's question is whether THAT
    shape works now. M10 measured temperature:0 -> 400 on opus; swe-2 was
    never isolated, so D2 doubles as the swe-2 field-isolation draw.

- D3 streaming chat on swe-2 (POST, body {"model":"swe-2","max_tokens":64,
  "stream":true,"stream_options":{"include_usage":true},"messages":
  [{"role":"user","content":COUNT_PROMPT}]}, timeout 320 s):
  Claim: HTTP 200 text/event-stream, content deltas present, usage block
    with completion_tokens > 0.
  Falsifier: timeout (cold-start class), non-200, or a stream with no
    content deltas and no usage.
  P(200 + content + usage) = 0.85 (streaming is the r18-proven path on
