## DEFECT-1 (harness, this seat) — TTFT not persisted in the seat stream run

/tmp/kengaku-r19-devin/probe_runner.py (draft rev) and the first seat2 revision
computed ttft only in code paths that never ran for the seat stream; the receipt
for [3/3] carries sse_lines/content/usage but no ttft_content_ms. The D5
prediction is therefore unprovable, not missed. Fixed in the runner before the
battery P4 run (span/TTFT persisted there: first_last_span_ms=0 captured on
P4(ii)); the seat's own D5 stays unprovable because a re-fire would spend a
second request against the one-attempt rule.

## SEAT ANSWER (the assignment's question)

"Model listing vs chat behavior — verify whether chat on the served model works now":
YES, chat works — via streaming (200, correct output, usage, alias swe-2->swe-2-high
confirmed live). The r18 non-stream shape (temperature:0) is refused with 400
invalid_argument in ~0.4 s; the r18 cold-start timeout did not reproduce on this
warm shim (unit uptime ~18 h, steady foreign traffic in the journal). GET /models
200 here coexists with a WORKING chat path — the inverse of the r18 token-plan
keys, where /models 200 coexisted with a dead chat path. Both directions of the
r18 headline are now evidenced: listing is neither sufficient (token-plan) nor
necessary (this shim's static list omits claude-opus-5-5-high, which M10 showed
answers 200) for chat usability.

